# {{.Name}} ({{.Type}})

Manages a single Homebrew formula or cask.

With the default `ignore_version = true`, the resource manages package
presence and install reason without planning upgrades for newer Homebrew
candidates. Exact `version` values are still enforced when configured.

`install_reason` is both desired and observed state. Formulae are kept as
`on_request` so Homebrew does not treat them as dependency-only packages
eligible for autoremove. If external Homebrew operations change a formula to
`dependency`, refresh records the drift and the next apply marks it as
requested again. Casks always report `on_request`.

